    setup: {
      players: 'One player. Terrace is a solitaire (two-deck patience) for a single player.',
      deck: 'Two standard 52-card decks shuffled together (104 cards).',
      equipment: 'Two decks, table space for reserve, eight foundations, nine tableaus, stock and discard.',
      dealing: 'Shuffle both decks. Lay 11 cards face-up in a row as the reserve. Below, eight empty foundation piles and nine empty tableau piles. Deal three cards from stock face-up, one to each of three tableaus. Choose one of these three to move to the first foundation; only cards of that rank may start other empty foundations. Deal seven more cards from stock, one onto each remaining empty tableau. Remaining cards form the stock (face-up, squared). Discard pile starts empty.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. Layout: 11-card reserve (face-up), eight foundations, nine tableaus, stock, discard. 2. Building: Foundations build up in alternating colors (red and black), circular order with Ace between King and 2, 13 cards per foundation. Tableaus build down in alternating colors. 3. Empty tableau rule: When any tableau is empty, it must be filled immediately with a card from the stock or the discard. 4. When no tableaus are empty (or stock and discard are both empty): top cards of tableaus may move to other tableaus or foundations; top card of reserve to foundations only; top card of stock or discard to tableaus or foundations. 5. Dealing: Play one card from the stock to the discard pile at any time, except when there is an empty tableau.',
